 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Laughing at how movies stuff product placement into every scene, Max, Fedya, and Senya hold up a bottle of cooking oil like actors in a commercial before debating their favorite film genres.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Федя, дай мне масло.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Пожалуйста, вот твоё масло.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "О, это моё любимое масло!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ну да, всё правильно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Потом в кинотеатре мы плюёмся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "А потом снимают вторую часть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Арсений у нас настоящий кинокритик.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А сам ты что смотришь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вот молоток уже освободился.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо, мне уже не нужен.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я люблю хорошее мужское кино.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ненавижу эти скучные понедельники.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's walk through the product-placement parody line by line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Федя, дай мне масло.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Fedya, give me the oil.' Admitting that Fedya should give him the oil shows Max being honest for a change.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Пожалуйста, вот твоё масло.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here you go, here is your oil.' Since here Max goes here is Max's oil, Fedya does not waste words on excuses.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "О, это моё любимое масло!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, this is my favorite oil!' Max declares that this is his favorite oil as the tension in the room peaks. Russian drops \"is\" in the present, setting the two halves of the thought side by side.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ну да, всё правильно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well yes, that is exactly right.' Saying that that is exactly right is how Senya sets the tone with Fedya.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Потом в кинотеатре мы плюёмся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Then at the movie theater we spit in disgust.' With the situation and conversation in play, Senya keeps this short reply brisk and direct.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "А потом снимают вторую часть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And then they film a second part.' Around the situation and work, Senya sets a calm, everyday tone with Fedya.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Арсений у нас настоящий кинокритик.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Our Arseny is a real film critic.' Fedya mentions that their is a real film critic so Max sees what is at stake. In Russian you say \"by me\" or \"with us\" rather than \"I have\", so the situation sits right with the person.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А сам ты что смотришь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And what do you watch yourself?' By wondering what Max watches themselves, Fedya presses Max for a straight answer.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вот молоток уже освободился.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here, the meat mallet is free now.' Pointing out that here the meat mallet is free now gives Fedya a sobering reality check.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо, мне уже не нужен.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Thanks, I do not need it anymore.' Noting that he does not need it anymore keeps Max's side of the story simple and clear.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я люблю хорошее мужское кино.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I love a good manly movie.' Admitting that he loves a good manly movie shows Senya being honest for a change.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ненавижу эти скучные понедельники.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I hate these boring Mondays.' Hating these boring is how Senya lays out the situation for Fedya. Now listen to the whole exchange again at natural speed.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Федя, дай мне масло.",
